    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Maths feels like a practical tool more than an abstract exercise. As someone who enjoys problem-solving through hobbies like cooking or cycling (which require measuring and balancing), I find algebra’s structured logic refreshing. It’s less about memorization—more about understanding relationships between ideas. That said, the maths hat subject is where I sometimes struggle with its complexity; it demands precision even when my openness score suggests I’d rather explore creative analogies first.",
